#: src/apps/notifications/presentation/live.py
msgid ""
"Recipient-only SSE invalidations over the persisted unified inbox. Requires an active bearer "
"access token, user, session and registered client. No query parameters or user_id are accepted. "
"Native EventSource needs an authenticated Node proxy; direct clients use streaming fetch with "
"Authorization. Subscribe then refresh inbox/search and inbox/unread on inbox.resync, on reconnect"
" and at least every 60 seconds. Last-Event-ID is an optional bounded reconnect hint, not an "
"authorized replay cursor. inbox.changed contains only schema_version and notification_ref_id; its"
" SSE id is the same reference. Deduplicate ids and coalesce refreshes. No subject, business data,"
" password, URL or error is streamed. Heartbeat and authorization checks have a 15-second cadence;"
" authorization probes are bounded to 3 seconds and changed events recheck authorization before "
"sending. A stream lasts at most 300 seconds, receives at most 256 signals, and times out blocked "
"sends after 5 seconds. Limit 3 streams per recipient and 200 per configured cache namespace "
"across processes. No stream-long database session. Offline/missed signals remain in persisted "
"search. Authentication or service failure after headers closes the stream; pre-stream errors use "
"existing JSON envelopes. Success is text/event-stream, never a JSON success envelope. Private no-"
"store/no-transform; proxies must disable buffering/compression and propagate disconnects. This "
"backend contract does not establish browser or Node proxy acceptance."
msgstr ""
"Recipient-only SSE invalidations over the persisted unified inbox. Requires an active bearer "
"access token, user, session and registered client. No query parameters or user_id are accepted. "
"Native EventSource needs an authenticated Node proxy; direct clients use streaming fetch with "
"Authorization. Subscribe then refresh inbox/search and inbox/unread on inbox.resync, on reconnect"
" and at least every 60 seconds. Last-Event-ID is an optional bounded reconnect hint, not an "
"authorized replay cursor. inbox.changed contains only schema_version and notification_ref_id; its"
" SSE id is the same reference. Deduplicate ids and coalesce refreshes. No subject, business data,"
" password, URL or error is streamed. Heartbeat and authorization checks have a 15-second cadence;"
" authorization probes are bounded to 3 seconds and changed events recheck authorization before "
"sending. A stream lasts at most 300 seconds, receives at most 256 signals, and times out blocked "
"sends after 5 seconds. Limit 3 streams per recipient and 200 per configured cache namespace "
"across processes. No stream-long database session. Offline/missed signals remain in persisted "
"search. Authentication or service failure after headers closes the stream; pre-stream errors use "
"existing JSON envelopes. Success is text/event-stream, never a JSON success envelope. Private no-"
"store/no-transform; proxies must disable buffering/compression and propagate disconnects. This "
"backend contract does not establish browser or Node proxy acceptance."

